  "definitions": {
    "0": "For every real x, x^2 >= 0, so sqrt(x^2) has domain R.",
    "1": "For every x >= 0, sqrt(x^2) = x, including zero.",
    "3": "For every x < 0, sqrt(x^2) = -x.",
    "5": "For all real x, sqrt(x^2) = |x|; the radical is the nonnegative principal root, not both signed roots."
